Well, my agenda is different than yours. I want my
XL:1 at top level Sokoban, because the treasure zoo
monster population is generated when I arrive and in
part with difficulty in response to my XL. I want
that zoo, with its many monsters, to be within the
capacity of the crowd of pets I've usually
accumulated by then, despite that I can't reach them
to heal them while they fight in their, and I want
me to remain at XL:1 when the fighting is done
because at least half the time, I've still got the
protection racket going.

None of this is particularly in pursuit of
ascending, as noted elsewhere, I shelve games where
I'm in any danger of ascending. It just keeps the
game fun and my skills continuously being honed.

> No giants, no too tough monsters in the zoo.

That depends on "too tough for whom". Maxed out
domestic animals seem to run out of steam about the
lecrotta level, so it doesn't take much XL increase
by you to put them out of contention as your main
fighting force. If you hit Sokoban at DLVL:10 with
you at XL:10, four levels up you're going to find a
treasure zoo with monster difficulty up to 8, and a
swarm of monsters that tough can take out your HD:9
domestic pets pretty fast. More than that, you'll
likely be gaining experience on the way up just
because your pets are even worse equipped to handle
the the monster difficulties your XL has created in
the lower levels of Sokoban, so you might gain a
level or even (barely conceivably) two levels from
DLVL:10 to toplevel Sokoban, worsening the situation
more. I _really_, _really_ don't want to meet a huge
bunch of mean humanoids with nasty wands just at the
point my pets start saying "after you, master". That
hallway isn't enough protection, wand zaps reach
right out and touch you, and the amulet you want is
on the other side of the Zoo.

